Review my code and apply a helpful tip from @bk201- from one of his recent PR-reviews:

>  In JS you have never be sure that error is instance of Error. It might be string, number, object, any type. I prefer use the following code taking into consideration that TS is type paranoid
const message = error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error)

I accidentally stumbled upon this. A long time ago I attached several MongoDB RU accounts directly to my workspace for testing. Over time focused on other things I didn't notice that they disappeared until I started investigating something else and discovered that they are still stored but will be ignored here: https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-cosmosdb/blob/0d5a89a85681862732c4c68a46d0002dc4aacf83/src/tree/workspace-view/cosmosdb/CosmosDBWorkspaceItem.ts#L89-L90
@tnaum-ms did we miss to implement some migration path after adding Clusters support and moving Mongo RU to the new codebase?

This is how the items are structured:
```
{
  id: "sevoku-mongo.mongo.cosmos.azure.com:10255",
  name: "sevoku-mongo.mongo.cosmos.azure.com:10255",
  properties: {
    isEmulator: false,
    api: "MongoDB",
  },
  secrets: [
    "mongodb://sevoku-mongo:[secret]@sevoku-mongo.mongo.cosmos.azure.com:10255/?ssl=true&replicaSet=globaldb&retrywrites=false&maxIdleTimeMS=120000&appName=@sevoku-mongo@",
  ],
}
```

`isEmulator` is obsolete there because resource items are always tied to a subscription.

              @tnaum-ms this should be dropped, we now have dedicated support for emulator nodes

_Originally posted by @tnaum-ms in https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-cosmosdb/pull/2557#discussion_r1957112418_

A user reported issues with MongoDB query operators, including `$gt`, `$lt`, `$exists`, etc., not working as expected. An example query provided by the user indicated that specific operators did not return the expected results.  

```json
{
  "correlationId": "123456",
  "resultEnum": {
    "$gt": 1
  }
}
```

**Task:**  
- Reproduce the reported issue.  
- Investigate the root cause, if verified.  
- Fix the issue and ensure that all standard MongoDB query operators work as expected.
